{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"agent_message","text":"The peer review exposed one real presentation defect in the first render: unequal facet sizes made the two-column chart cramped and truncated long labels. The single allowed revision now uses one vertically stacked, free-height facet per attribute, preserves the package’s declared level order, keeps attribute-specific reference lines, and clarifies in the caption that the repeat is excluded. I am not adding Claude’s suggested chi-square tests because the brief asks for a descriptive frequency check and the assignment-dependence assumptions needed for that inferential null are not specified."}}
